{"ts": 1793978033.2225425, "run_id": "bsa_serial_dilution__driver_only__claude-haiku-5-5__r3__64d485446022", "source": "agent", "event": "run_started", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "layers": {"name": "driver_only", "prompt_rules": false, "driver_enforcement": true}, "prompt": "Make a two-fold serial dilution of the BSA standard across assay_plate wells A1 to A4, so that A1 is 2 mg/mL, A2 is 1 mg/mL, A3 is 0.5 mg/mL and A4 is 0.25 mg/mL, with 100 uL in each well. Dilute with PBS buffer.\n", "system_prompt": "You operate a laboratory bench through tools. The bench has a liquid handler and an absorbance plate reader.\n\n- Call list_devices to see the deck: the labware, and the named containers with their contents. Call describe_device for details of one device.\n- Containers are named '<labware>:<well>', for example 'assay_plate:B3'. Tip spots are named like 'tips:A1'.\n- The liquid handler has one channel. Pick up a tip, aspirate, dispense, then drop the tip.\n- Physical actions run on real equipment and cannot be undone.\n\nWhen you have finished, reply with a short summary of what you did."}
